  "RightSideDisplay": 10,
  "RightSideHtmlBlock": "<h4>Expressions of likelihood</h4><p>State how likely the assessed event or development is, using one of the terms below, and explain the basis in the comments: the logic and evidence, the quantity and quality of sources, and your understanding of the topic. Don't mix terms from different rows, and don't put a confidence level and a degree of likelihood in the same sentence.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><th>Term</th><th>Or</th><th>Probability</th></tr><tr><td>almost no chance</td><td>remote</td><td>01-05%</td></tr><tr><td>very unlikely</td><td>highly improbable</td><td>05-20%</td></tr><tr><td>unlikely</td><td>improbable (improbably)</td><td>20-45%</td></tr><tr><td>roughly even chance</td><td>roughly even odds</td><td>45-55%</td></tr><tr><td>likely</td><td>probable (probably)</td><td>55-80%</td></tr><tr><td>very likely</td><td>highly probable</td><td>80-95%</td></tr><tr><td>almost certain(ly)</td><td>nearly certain</td><td>95-99%</td></tr></table><p><i>Source: Intelligence Community Directive 203, Analytic Standards (ODNI, 2015, as amended 2022), section D.6.e.(2). ICD 203 does not define confidence levels, so this model does not score confidence.</i></p>",
